# HTML & Accessibility Rules

- Use semantic HTML: `<main>`, `<label>`, `<input>`, `<button>`, result container.
- Always pair inputs with `<label for="...">`.
- Ensure keyboard usability:
  - Button is focusable
  - Enter key should submit/reverse if placed in a `<form>`.
- Display result in an element with `aria-live="polite"` so screen readers announce updates.
- Keep HTML minimal. No inline JS.